// Corpse-preservation utility: "halts all rot and corruption... no foul
// power can rouse the corpse into undeath." No combat effect (sheet's own
// classification), and unlike death_armor.ron/revivify.ron there is no
// living-ally target to redirect an `attack_effect` onto either -- the
// target here is an inert corpse, which has no addressable entity/state in
// this engine to touch at all (no "preserved/ward against reanimation" flag
// exists on any body). `SelfBuff` with an empty buff list is therefore not a
// simplification of a touch-ally delivery (contrast spare_the_dying.ron) --
// it is the correct, and only, primitive: a flavor-only cast with no
// mechanical target. Same NO-OP-placeholder shape already shipped for
// Axiomancy's own non-combat utility casts (see
// assets/common/abilities/spells/axiomancy/immovable_object.ron and
// wristpocket.ron).
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    buffs: [],
    energy_cost: 20,
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Divine)),
)
